Behavior proved: the AgentRuntime registry rejects provider handles whose initial status is `stopping` or `offline`, disposes the rejected handle, and does not publish an invalid activation event. It also suppresses duplicate status edges and rejects invalid later lifecycle transitions without emitting them. Host and SDK artifact-list routes forward `afterCursor` and `limit` to `listArtifactsPage()`; artifact visibility and ambiguity filtering remain provider-owned, while artifact byte reads retain their exact-reference lookup path. Browser, separate-host, and independent ACP recovery scope remains open.
